r\\frac{4}{3}\\right\\rfloor + 4 \\bmod 3 = 1 + 1 = 2$$$ "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As an answer, obviously, $$$f_3(2)$$$ and $$$f_3(4)$$$ are suitable."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1650B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1650/problem/B"}